---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro'
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_DOMAIN } from '../../config/site'
---
<Page title="Privacy policy" kicker="Legal" lead="What we collect, why, and the choices you have. Short version: very little, and we never sell it." updated="October 10, 2026" prose>
  <p>This policy explains how the Laravel & VueJs project (“we”, “us”) handles personal information on <strong>{SITE_DOMAIN}</strong> (the “Site”).</p>
  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No accounts.</strong> The Site is static. There is no sign-up, and we do not store passwords or profiles.</li>
    <li><strong>Server logs.</strong> Our hosting provider, Cloudflare, processes technical data such as IP addresses and browser information to deliver and protect the Site. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Emails you send us.</strong> If you contact us or ask to join the newsletter, we receive your email address and message, and use them only to reply or to send the newsletter.</li>
    <li><strong>Your preferences.</strong> Your light or dark theme choice is saved in your browser's local storage. It never leaves your device.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Comments</h2>
  <p>Comments are provided by Disqus and are only loaded when you click “Load comments”. Once loaded, Disqus may set cookies and process data under the <a href="https://disqus.com/privacy-policy/">Disqus privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
  <p>We do not run analytics or advertising trackers at the moment. If we add them in the future, we will update this page first and, where the law requires it, ask for your consent.</p>
  <h2>Social networks</h2>
  <p>Share buttons are plain links: nothing is sent to a social network until you click one. Our pages and groups on Facebook, X, LinkedIn, Instagram, Telegram and Pinterest are governed by those platforms' own policies.</p>
  <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
  <p>We keep emails only as long as needed to handle your request, and newsletter addresses until you unsubscribe.</p>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR or California law), you can ask to access, correct or delete the personal information we hold about you, or object to its use. We do not sell personal information. To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>The Site is meant for developers and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect their personal information.</p>
  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>
</Page>
